Across the three Qwen benchmark aggregates, moving to the compressed arm shifts accuracy by at most 0.44 points in either direction.
A uniform-timestamp control on pooled LongVideoBench long videos moves by 0.31 points ($p{=}.784$), which shows the stability is a property of the compression, not something special about OMP-selected frames.

